/*
 * Reference: how Wi-Fi credentials are stored, for development convenience.
 *
 * The firmware DOES NOT include this file and DOES NOT read a compiled-in
 * header any more. The production path is:
 *
 *     provisioning portal  ->  NVS  ->  station mode
 *
 * This file is kept only to document the NVS layout, which is useful when you
 * want to pre-seed a board for bench testing or inspect/clear what the portal
 * stored.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * NVS namespace: "wifi"          (the layout used by 78/esp-wifi-connect)
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *   key "ssid"       string, up to 32 bytes, first (preferred) network
 *   key "password"   string, up to 64 bytes
 *   key "ssid1"      string, second network
 *   key "password1"  string
 *   ...
 *   key "ssid9"      string, up to ten saved networks
 *   key "password9"  string
 *
 * The station scans for access points and matches them against this list, so
 * saving several networks lets the board roam by itself.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Inspecting and clearing
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *   - from the camera's serial console:  clearwifi
 *   - from the camera's status page:     not exposed (deliberate, one method)
 *   - from a PC with the board attached:
 *       python -m esptool --chip esp32s3 -p <port> erase-region 0x9000 0x4000
 *     (wipes the whole NVS partition, including anything else stored there)
 *
 * There is no plain-text credentials file in this repository. Credentials are
 * typed into the captive portal on the phone and land in NVS on the device.
 */
